  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Amentum Technology has $492M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Amentum Technology won 126 awards so far, with an average award size of $3.9M, and obligations are up 13.3% year over year. Obligations peaked earlier in the five-year series at $1.2B in FY21 and FY22, then declined to $947M in FY23, $600M in FY24, and $434M in FY25 before reaching $492M in FY26. The largest single buyer so far is the National Aeronautics and Space Administration at $290M, followed by the Department of Defense at $189M. Engineering Services and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) are the top markets at $198M and $192M respectively, with Facilities Support Services at $97M. The dataset also shows smaller entries such as General Services Administration at $8.5M and markets with zero or negative entries, including Other Computer Related Services at $0 and Computer Systems Design Services at -$3.5M.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has Amentum Technology’s obligation profile changed over time?",
        "body": "Amentum Technology’s obligations were $1.2B in FY21 and $1.2B in FY22, then moved to $947M in FY23, $600M in FY24, $434M in FY25, and $492M in FY26. Amentum Technology’s FY2026 to date obligations are up 13.3% year over year compared with the prior fiscal-year-to-date figure. The multi-year series shows a decline from the FY21/FY22 peak into FY25 before the FY26 uptick."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who pays Amentum Technology and which markets dominate its awards?",
        "body": "National Aeronautics and Space Administration is the largest buyer at $290M, followed by the Department of Defense at $189M and the General Services Administration at $8.5M. Engineering Services and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) are the leading markets at $198M and $192M, with Facilities Support Services at $97M."
      }
    ]
